{title: Blessed Assurance}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby (1820-1915)}
{key: D}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[D]Blessed as[G]surance, [D]Jesus is [A]mine!
[D]O what a [Bm]foretaste of [E]glory di[A]vine!
[D]Heir of sal[G]vation, [D]purchase of God,
[G]Born of His Spirit, [A]washed in His [D]blood.
{eov}

{soc}
This is my [D]story, [G]this is my [D]song,
Praising my [G]Savior [E]all the day [A]long;
This is my [D]story, [G]this is my [D]song,
Praising my [G]Savior [A]all the day [D]long.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 2}
[D]Perfect sub[G]mission, [D]perfect de[A]light,
[D]Visions of [Bm]rapture now [E]burst on my [A]sight;
[D]Angels de[G]scending [D]bring from a[Bm]bove
[G]Echoes of mercy, [A]whispers of [D]love.
{eov}

{soc}
This is my [D]story, [G]this is my [D]song,
Praising my [G]Savior [E]all the day [A]long;
This is my [D]story, [G]this is my [D]song,
Praising my [G]Savior [A]all the day [D]long.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 3}
[D]Perfect sub[G]mission, [D]all is at [A]rest,
[D]I in my [Bm]Savior am [E]happy and [A]blest,
[D]Watching and [G]waiting, [D]looking a[Bm]bove,
[G]Filled with His goodness, [A]lost in His [D]love.
{eov}

{soc}
This is my [D]story, [G]this is my [D]song,
Praising my [G]Savior [E]all the day [A]long;
